title: Niko4
---
<<declare $playerName="player">>
<<gatherVars>>
Here you were at the library again. It felt almost mechanical, the way your
feet brought you here without thought.

Somewhere deep down, you longed to see Niko. To hear his thoughts again.
There was something about the way he spoke that pulled at you, something
dark and fascinating that made you want to know everything about him.

As usual, he sat at the same secluded table tucked into the corner.

His eyes met yours before you could even speak.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Have you come for more pestering?"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He greeted you with a lopsided smile, closing his book. The cover was a
limited edition of Frankenstein, one you'd admired before.

You: "Is it any good?"

You gestured toward the book as you set your bag down.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "I don't mind it. Shelley makes interesting points about abandonment
and nature versus nurture."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

You: "I don't believe in the nature versus nurture argument."

You turned your nose up slightly.

You: "Everyone has a choice to act differently. Some have it easier, but in
the end everything comes down to choice. Though the debate is fascinating.
Don't..."

You trailed off as his intense glare made you shiver.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Not everything is a choice."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

His tone was sharp, almost angry.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Some things are beyond a person's control. If they had a choice, they
would have chosen differently."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He slammed his book onto the table. The sound echoed through the library,
drawing a few glances from nearby students.

You felt uneasy, realizing you had upset him.

-> Apologise profusely
    <<incRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump ApologiseN4>>
-> Pull out books and ignore it
    <<jump PullBooks>>
-> Ask what's wrong
    <<decRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump AskN4>>
===

title: ApologiseN4
---
You: "I'm so sorry."

The apology came out quickly.

You: "Please, don't be mad at me. I would never want to upset you."

You reached for his hands, hoping to show your sincerity.

You: "I'm sorry."

You repeated, more quietly.

<<jump EndNiko4>>
===

title: PullBooks
---
Unsure how to fix things, you quietly placed your books on the table.

Ignoring his reaction seemed safest.

You: "So... I have another question for you."

<<jump EndNiko4>>
===

title: AskN4
---
You: "I can't apologise for something I don't understand."

You kept your voice steady.

You: "If I did, it wouldn't mean anything."

You took a breath before continuing.

You: "What's wrong?"

Niko looked genuinely surprised, as if no one had asked him that before.

For a moment, something shifted in him.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "I lost my parents in a car accident."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "I was too young. I don't remember their faces."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "It wasn't their choice to die. It was the choice of a drunk driver."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "I'm glad he's dead."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

You felt sick hearing it.

Suddenly, everything about him made sense.

Their death wasn't a choice, and neither was how it shaped him.

<<jump EndNiko4>>
===

title: EndNiko4
---
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Forget it. Ask your damn question. I'm over this."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He shoved the paper into your hands.

Without another word, he grabbed his things and stormed out.

You were left alone, unsettled and filled with guilt for what you might
have caused.
===